# Copy to .env in this same folder and adjust for your machine.
# Never commit the real .env — it's gitignored.

POSTGRES_DB=setu
POSTGRES_USER=setu
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=setu_dev_password
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

REDIS_PORT=6379

KAFKA_PORT=9092

PROMETHEUS_PORT=9091
GRAFANA_PORT=3001
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin

# --- Containerised services (docker-compose.services.yml) ---
# All three are secrets: generate your own, never commit them.
#   JWT_SIGNING_KEY       the Identity service's token-signing key:  node backend/tools/generate-jwt-key.js
#   SETU_INTERNAL_TOKEN   shared by the services for calls the gateway never routes (guardian confirmation, AI facts):  any long random string
#   METRICS_SCRAPE_TOKEN  what Prometheus presents to /actuator/prometheus on every service:  any long random string
# JWT_SIGNING_KEY=…
# SETU_INTERNAL_TOKEN=…
# METRICS_SCRAPE_TOKEN=…
# The advisor's model (without a key it starts on the local Ollama model and says so):
# GEMINI_API_KEY=…
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# A hosted fallback model on NVIDIA (build.nvidia.com), tried after the second Gemini model and before the local one. Off without a key.
# Set it with: pwsh infra/scripts/set-nvidia-key.ps1 (it asks for the key without showing it).
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-…
# NVIDIA_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct   (a model with tool calling)
# Online fee payment through Razorpay (test keys from the Razorpay dashboard, rzp_test_..., move no money). Without them online payment is off:
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_…
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=…
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=…   the secret you type when creating the webhook (URL: <public address>/finance/provider-webhooks/razorpay)
# Which database the services use (created on first start); a fresh one lets the demo data seed itself:
# SETU_DB_NAME=setu_demo
# JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=…   the public half of JWT_SIGNING_KEY (not a secret): the core process verifies Identity's tokens with it. Derive it:
#   node -e "const c=require('crypto');console.log(c.createPublicKey(c.createPrivateKey({key:Buffer.from(process.env.K,'base64'),format:'der',type:'pkcs8'})).export({type:'spki',format:'der'}).toString('base64'))"   (K=the private key)
